1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:05,283
An agent just opened a pull request. Do
you ship it today?

2
00:00:06,883 --> 00:00:10,807
Most teams either rubber stamp the diff or
rewrite the whole thing.

3
00:00:12,357 --> 00:00:15,910
Three checks catch almost everything an
agent gets wrong.

4
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:18,923
Sixty seconds.

5
00:00:20,473 --> 00:00:23,085
Forty seconds reading the diff properly.

6
00:00:24,055 --> 00:00:29,314
Ten seconds running it, and ten asking
what it quietly refuses to handle.

7
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:34,847
Wire those checks to one command, so the
machine runs them.

8
00:00:36,397 --> 00:00:37,836
Green means merge.

9
00:00:38,806 --> 00:00:40,513
Red means send it back.

10
00:00:42,063 --> 00:00:45,534
Three checks. One command. A minute of
your time.

11
00:00:47,084 --> 00:00:51,821
Pick one repository this week. Run the
checks. That is the method.
